  "id": "DrugBank_DB01601 - MONDO_12268",
  "verbalization": "Lopinavir, through its indication for HIV Infectious Disease, is linked to Aids via a chain of indications that involve antiretroviral therapies. The evidence suggests that Lopinavir may be repurposed for the treatment of HIV-related conditions, with its use in combination with other drugs like Elvitegravir, Zalcitabine, and Doravirine, all of which are indicated for Aids. These drugs are part of a class of antiretroviral agents that target different stages of the HIV life cycle, potentially offering a therapeutic pathway for the treatment of AIDS. The shared indication for HIV Infectious Disease across these drugs implies a common therapeutic goal, which may support the repurposing of Lopinavir for Aids. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a potential role for Lopinavir in the management of HIV-related conditions, with the underlying mechanism likely involving antiretroviral activity.",
